  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "OnUpdateFiberStackSize",
    "file": "php-src/Zend/zend.c",
    "description": "`OnUpdateFiberStackSize` stores `fiber.stack_size` using `zend_ini_parse_quantity_warn()` directly into `EG(fiber_stack_size)` (a `size_t`) without rejecting negative values. Input `\"-1\"` is converted to a huge unsigned size, which propagates into fiber creation. In `zend_fiber_init_context`/`zend_fiber_stack_allocate` this oversized value leads to invalid stack/top calculations and a bogus stack pointer passed to `make_fcontext`, which then performs a write to an invalid address (crash at `make_x86_64_sysv_elf_gas.S:69`).",
    "conditions": "PoV sets `ini_set(\"fiber.stack_size\", \"-1\")`, then creates and starts a Fiber. Data flow: INI string -> `OnUpdateFiberStackSize` (no range check, signed-to-unsigned wrap) -> `EG(fiber_stack_size)` -> `zend_fiber_init_context(..., EG(fiber_stack_size))` -> `zend_fiber_stack_allocate` / stack pointer arithmetic -> `make_fcontext` writes through invalid computed context pointer. Trigger requires attacker-controlled negative `fiber.stack_size` and execution of `Fiber::start()`."
  },
